Same starting body (3,4) (3,3) (3,2), same RIGHT move, but this time food is sitting at (3,5). What is the body afterwards?,"(3,5) (3,4) (3,3) - the tail still moves because the head advanced","(3,5) (3,4) (3,3) (3,2) - four segments, because the eating branch never removes the tail","(3,5) (3,4) (3,3) (3,2) (3,1) - the snake grows by two","(3,4) (3,3) (3,2) - the snake pauses for one move while eating",,2,"Identical to the previous move except that the tail (3,2) survives. Comparing the two answers side by side is the clearest way to see growth as an omission rather than an action.",2

