The condition is:

    boolean bitesItself = occupied.contains(newHead) && !(newHead.equals(tail));

Stated in plain language, when does the snake die from this check?,"Whenever the new head is anywhere on the snake, including the tail",When the new head lands on any part of the snake EXCEPT the tail cell - moving onto the tail is allowed because the tail is leaving that cell on this same move,Only when the new head lands exactly on the tail,Only when the snake is longer than three segments,,2,"The exception is not that the tail is special, but that the tail cell is about to be empty. Every other segment stays exactly where it is during this move.",2

