In the non-eating branch, the order is: pollLast, remove(tail), addFirst, add(newHead). An earlier version added the head first and removed the tail afterwards. On a two-segment snake with head (2,3) and tail (3,3) moving DOWN onto its own tail, the old order left body with 2 entries but occupied with only 1. What went wrong?,addFirst silently failed because the cell was taken,"occupied.add(newHead) did nothing, since (3,3) was already in the Set as the tail

