The eating branch calls spawnFood() BEFORE notifyScoreChanged(). What would a listener see if those two lines were swapped?,The same thing - listeners only receive the score,"The same score either way, but a listener that also queried game.getFoodPosition() during the callback would see the OLD food position, which the snake is already standing on",The score would be one food behind,The listener would be notified twice,,2,"Callbacks fire in the middle of an operation, so what a listener can observe depends on how much of the update has already happened. Notifying only once the object is fully consistent avoids exposing a half-finished state.",2

