Which of these statements about a single call to performMove() are true? (select all that apply),The body always gains exactly one head cell unless the game ends,The Set and the Deque always end the call holding the same cells,The tail is removed on every move without exception,The score can change on a move where the length does not,A move that ends the game leaves the body unchanged,"1,2,5","The tail survives when eating, which is growth. Score and length always change together, since both happen only in the eating branch. And both endGame() paths return before any mutation, so a fatal move leaves no trace on the snake.",2
